# "Whenever you cast a multicolored instant or sorcery spell from your hand, exile that spell instead of putting it into your
# graveyard as it resolves. If you do, it becomes plotted." Bot1 casts Lilah on turn 1 and on turn 3 a Lightning Helix from the
# hand: the Helix does its damage and life gain first (Bot2 takes 3, Bot1 gains 3), then is exiled instead of going to the
# graveyard and is plotted, so it can't be cast the turn it became plotted. On turn 5 Bot1 casts it from exile without paying
# its mana cost (Bot2 takes 3 more); that cast is not from the hand, so only prowess triggers (Lilah's own trigger is not put on
# the stack with it) and the Helix goes to the graveyard. Prowess is on: the Helix, a
# noncreature spell, makes Lilah 4/4 until end of turn.

